{title: Do You Love Me}
{subtitle: Luke 5:1–11; Matthew 14:25–33; Luke 22:54–62; John 21:15–19}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb/D] | [Cm7] [Ebmaj7/Bb] | [Ab] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
All night [Eb]we fished on Gennesaret and [Cm7]the nets came up bare
He said [Ab]put out into the deep [Bb]and let them down from there
So full of [Eb]fish the nets were tearing, both [Cm7]boats began to sink
I [Ab]fell down at his knees and I could [Bb]hardly speak or think
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Simon son of [Cm7]John, do you love [Ab]me
Yes, Lord
You know that I [Bb]love you
Feed my [Eb]lambs
Take care of my [Cm7]sheep
Follow [Ab]me, follow [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]In the fourth watch of the [Cm7]night we saw him walking on the sea
[Ab]I asked him, call me out to you, [Bb]and Come, he said to me
[Eb]I walked on the water till [Cm7]I saw how strong the wind could be
[Ab]Then sinking down I cried, Lord, save [Bb]me, and he reached his hand to [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Simon son [Cm7]of John, do you love [Ab]me
Yes, Lord
You know that I [Bb]love you
Feed my [Eb]lambs
Take care of my [Cm7]sheep
Follow [Ab]me, follow [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]By the fire in the courtyard a [Cm7]servant girl looked at my face
I [Ab]don't know him, I said, [Bb]three times I fell from grace
[Eb]The rooster crowed, the Lord turned [Cm7]round and looked straight at me
And [Ab]I went out into the night and [Bb]wept so bitterly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Three times I said I don't [Bb]know him
[Ab]Three times he asked [Bb]me, do [Ab]you love me
Lord, you know [Bb]everything
You know that I love [Eb]you
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Simon son of [Cm7]John, do you love [Ab]me
Yes, Lord
You know that I [Bb]love you
Feed my [Eb]lambs
Take care of my [Cm7]sheep
Follow [Ab]me, follow [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Follow [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
